1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:08,508
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,635
- ♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,143
I don't like Uno that way.

7
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,186
[Denden] <i>So, Gavin is really your bet?</i>

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,312
[in English] So, you're dumping me?!

9
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:23,690
I think it's not fair to you
to enter a relationship

10
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:25,066
where the guy is already
half-hearted with you.

11
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,109
So, it is Karla then?

12
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:27,736
[Cathy] <i>Just be together.</i>

13
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:28,862
Your new mission.

14
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,740
Rizaldo Coloma, the mayor who's in hiding?

15
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:34,242
[in English] The corrupt mayor,
bagman of senators.

16
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:35,618
[Mercado] <i>You need to find him.</i>

17
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:37,537
[all cheering] Atoy! Atoy!

18
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,581
[Red] <i>That's your biggest mistake, Atoy.</i>

19
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:40,498
You showed yourself to me.

20
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,917
[Emerson]
<i>So, now you're the real daughter.</i>

21
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:44,043
All of it!

22
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:47,088
- [Ibyang] <i>The bullying Janine did to me.</i>
- [Emerson] <i>Bullying.</i>

23
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,132
I'll do the same to her!

24
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:50,425
[cackles]

25
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,093
Just kidding!

26
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:53,094
Don't move too much.

27
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:55,638
- Hi, Father! Ah, hello.
- Oh? Come on, eat.

28
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,766
So, you're hiding here.
That means Audrey is here too.

29
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:00,685
Oh, there.
That insect on your face is gone.

30
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:04,731
Yes, like a green firefly
that keeps moving.

31
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:05,857
[Father Peping] You didn't feel it?

32
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,609
Where are you going?

33
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,819
[Ibyang] <i>Let's not fight anymore, okay?</i>

34
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:11,946
[Atoy] <i>Didn't you see anyone else</i>
<i>here earlier?</i>

35
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,823
<i>It's like someone tried to kill me, eh.</i>

36
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,075
[Paldo] <i>This belongs to Red.</i>

37
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,744
- <i>I remember he used this before.</i>
- [Janine, in English] Uncle Red?

38
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:19,120
[groans]

39
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:20,246
- [Kurt] <i>Ibyang and Janine,</i>
- [in English] Get your filthy hands…

40
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,247
- <i>they've been taken.</i>
- [groans]

41
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:24,751
They were loaded into a black
SUV by a bald guy!

42
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:25,668
[in English] It's Red.

43
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,213
Where are the kids? Ibyang? Janine?

44
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:29,964
- They were abducted by Red.
- What?!

45
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,008
Do you know where your parents
might have taken the kids?

46
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,010
[Gavin] <i>I don't know, Brother Atoy.</i>

47
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:34,928
Red!

48
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,388
[Audrey, in English]
Red, where the hell are my daughters?!

49
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:39,599
Where are the kids?
Give me back the children!

50
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:41,768
I'll make these kids suffer.

51
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:43,561
I'll profit from them.

52
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,480
[Red on the phone] <i>I'll send you pictures.</i>

53
00:01:45,563 --> 00:01:47,398
<i>So you'll know where they're going.</i>

54
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:49,109
And what condition they're in.

55
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:50,777
No, no, no, no! Hello! No!

56
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:54,155
PREVIOUSLY

57
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,199
What do we do?

58
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:57,200
Call him.

59
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:00,036
He's not answering.

60
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:03,581
- [theme music fades]
- [Jona] Brother Kurt, are you okay?

61
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,792
- [man] You were hit hard.
- [Jona] That kick earlier was intense, eh.

62
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,127
[indistinct chatter]

63
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:08,628
Excuse me! It's heavy, heavy!

64
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:11,589
Oh! Skin and bones,
gone right away! [chuckles]

65
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,092
We already gave away all the food,
it's done.

66
00:02:15,343 --> 00:02:17,011
Ah, what's happening?

67
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,972
Is there trouble here again?

68
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:24,018
Ibyang and Janine were abducted
by… by Red Regalia.

69
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:25,270
What?! [gasps]

70
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:27,730
[Gavin] Karla!

71
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,649
[pensive music playing]

72
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:31,568
Your mother's been looking for you!

73
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,945
Do you know Janine and Ibyang are missing?

74
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:36,447
Eh, fool, they just told me, oh!

75
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:38,825
Eh, why does it sound like
you're blaming me?

76
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:41,077
Of course, I'm worried about you!

77
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:44,122
We! We're worried about you!

78
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,457
There's a kidnapping happening,
and you're still wandering around.

79
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,836
Wait, wait, wait.

80
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,338
You're a Regalia, right?

81
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,341
Jona, this is Red's child, right?

82
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:58,469
[heavy music playing]

83
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,430
That's right!

84
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:01,764
Yes, him!

85
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,474
[Siony] Ahh!

86
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,894
You don't know what your father did?!

87
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,855
Or maybe you're your father's spy?

88
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:10,273
[Jona] Truth!

89
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:12,483
Boy, you're banned here!

90
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:13,818
Your father is evil!

91
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,987
- [Jona] True! Right! Right, he's evil!
- [man] Get out! Yes!

92
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,196
[Nestor] Hey, Tisoy.

93
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,198
Aren't you going to do anything?

94
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:21,284
I don't know anything. I'm not--

95
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,453
- I'm not involved in that.
- Oh.

96
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:25,163
I already left our house.

97
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:27,081
Bring back the children!

98
00:03:27,165 --> 00:03:28,291
- [Siony] Yes.
- Where did you take them?!

99
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:30,627
Your father is a demon!

100
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,253
[Jona] Right! Demon!

101
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:34,589
- Yes! Your father is a demon!
- The children. My God!

102
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:35,632
[Karla] Wait.

103
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:37,926
Gavin didn't do anything wrong!

104
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:39,469
No, Karla!

105
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:43,556
Maybe if we lock him up,
they'll return the children!

106
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,474
Exchange of heads!

107
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:47,852
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait! Just wait!

108
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:49,812
Just wait!

109
00:03:50,521 --> 00:03:52,982
Gavin didn't do anything wrong.

110
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:59,072
In fact, he was with us when we rescued
Brother Atoy at the junkyard!

111
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,158
[tense music playing]

112
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,952
That's the truth.

113
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,331
[music fades]

114
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,415
So, they escaped.

115
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,668
[theme music playing]

116
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,188
[music swells]

117
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:37,568
[music fades]

118
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:39,570
Why did my parents turn out like that?

119
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:42,573
[pensive music playing]

120
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,033
[sighs] Sorry.

121
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,036
Gavin…

122
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,499
Good thing you didn't take after
your parents.

123
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,962
But let's focus first. We need…

124
00:04:57,130 --> 00:05:00,049
We need to know
where they could have taken the children.

125
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:06,055
Aunt Audrey, what if I just go home?

126
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,433
So, I can get close to Dad or even Mom!

127
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:10,476
Maybe I can get info
on where they took Ibyang and Janine!

128
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,895
No! I won't allow it, Gavin!

129
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,273
Red is no longer in his right mind!

130
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,608
He killed your grandfather!

131
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:20,987
There's nothing he can't do!

132
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,989
[in English] You're not going anywhere.

133
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:24,574
[suspicious music playing]

134
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:28,453
That's right. Gavin… they'll suspect more
if you do that. Right.

135
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,125
Maybe we'll find something in their house.

136
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,210
[in English] Documents…

137
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:39,422
Old property files.

138
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:43,760
Auntie, didn't you say you saw your dad's
human trafficking files?

139
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,928
Maybe you'll remember a clue there.

140
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,433
It's like…

141
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:52,393
Ah, I think I saw something, uhm…

142
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:54,479
[in English] Uhm, V-- V. Starts with a V.

143
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:55,897
Ve…

144
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,441
Ve-- Velora Bay!

145
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:01,360
[Audrey] Ve-- Velora Bay!

146
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:04,363
[tense music playing]

147
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:11,329
I can't find anything here.

148
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:13,581
[Lily] Wait.

149
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,750
- I can't find anything.
- Wait, wait.

150
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:16,793
[Atoy] Isn't there anything else?

151
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:19,170
Velora Bay, Velora Bay,
Velora Bay, Velora Bay.

152
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:21,130
Wait, wait. I think I saw that
on the laptop.

153
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,508
- [Uno] There's something?
- Wait.

154
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:26,469
Right, it's in--
it's in the classified data!

155
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:29,305
I need the laptop.

156
00:06:29,972 --> 00:06:30,973
[Uno] All right.

157
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:37,438
[music fades]

158
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:41,359
[suspicious music playing]

159
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:48,282
I asked Father Peping to hide this laptop
here before I went on the mission.

160
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,911
I'm sure, if things get tight…

161
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,206
they'll search my house for it.

162
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,376
Only the two of us know about this.

163
00:07:00,294 --> 00:07:02,922
Thank you very much for keeping it safe.

164
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,302
[sighs]

165
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:09,262
Complete?

166
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:14,809
- [music swells]
- [keyboard clacking]

167
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:16,102
[in English] There. This is the location.

168
00:07:19,313 --> 00:07:21,274
- [ominous music playing]
- [Atoy] That's a huge place, ah.

169
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:22,984
Where is that?

170
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,362
[Lily]
It's posing as a high-end beach resort,

171
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:29,365
but it's actually one of the big
concentration camps

172
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:31,325
of the terrorist group Obsidian.

173
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,619
They're also connected
to the Black Meridian group.

174
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:36,956
[Atoy, in English] Black Meridian.

175
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,627
That's the international
human trafficking syndicate.

176
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,504
[Lily, in English] Yeah. One and only.

177
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,174
It's hard to get in here.

178
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:47,884
[in English]
The island is heavily guarded.

179
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:50,011
They have state-of-the-art radar systems,

180
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:52,889
because of their large involvement
in illegal activities.

181
00:07:53,389 --> 00:07:56,767
So, no one gets in
without being detected by the sensors.

182
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:58,936
[in English] Whether by air or underwater.

183
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:00,938
So, what now?

184
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,857
If they were taken there, what do we do?

185
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,150
How do we get them out?!

186
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,737
[tense music playing]

187
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,947
No matter what happens,
I'll get our children back.

188
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:13,075
If this has to be my last mission,
I'll do it.

189
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,287
What matters, Atoy…

190
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:19,874
is that you bring the children
back safely.

191
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:21,959
[music fades]

192
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,753
Who owns that island?

193
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:28,966
[heavy music playing]

194
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:34,472
[Mercado, in English]
That is Mr. Edison Kalaf.

195
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:36,516
The owner of Velora Bay.

196
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:40,603
He owns multiple businesses
across the Philippines.

197
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,981
[sneaky music playing]

198
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:46,400
[in English] Big time!

199
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:58,996
Where is this?

200
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,542
[in English] According to our intel…

201
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:08,422
he has a club here that he often visits
at this time of the year.

202
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:12,426
Where is this club?

203
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:14,929
- I want to go there.
- [chuckles]

204
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:21,644
Well, it's not your ordinary club.
It's in Ermita.

205
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:24,564
It's different.

206
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:33,823
[cool upbeat music playing]

207
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,041
[Atoy, in English] Ah, beer for all!

208
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:27,001
Oh, no. Sorry, uh…

209
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:28,753
[Atoy] Mister Nestor can't.

210
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:30,421
Just juice, just one.

211
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:34,008
And, uh… chicharon bulaklak.

212
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:36,052
[Gavin ordering]

213
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:38,179
Sisig, sisig.

214
00:10:38,262 --> 00:10:39,889
Sisig, sisig, sisig.

215
00:10:39,972 --> 00:10:42,016
[indistinct chatter]

216
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,645
- [Paldo] Thank you.
- [Emerson] And, what else-- no.

217
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:47,688
[indistinct chatter]

218
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,030
[applauding]

219
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:00,660
[in English] Well, hello, hello!

220
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:03,788
Hi! And good evening!

221
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:07,625
Good evening
to all our guests for tonight!

222
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,752
[Trinity, in English]
Did you guys enjoy that one?

223
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:12,922
Yes! Amazing, isn't it?

224
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:13,881
[cheering]

225
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,341
All right!

226
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:18,594
But you'll surely enjoy
our upcoming event more--

227
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,097
The Reyna Royale Rumble!

228
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,723
[cheering]

229
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:30,481
[Trinity, in English] To our regulars,
you already know what this is.

230
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:32,817
Because we do this annually.

231
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,527
[chuckles]

232
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,528
Oh, right?

233
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:40,825
But to our newcomers,
I see a lot of newcomers.

234
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:41,992
Yes.

235
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:44,578
This is a special event.

236
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:49,125
Okay, where groups will battle
in drag performances,

237
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:55,798
[Trinity] consisting of five to six
beautiful drag queens.

238
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:57,258
- [man whoops]
- [cheering]

239
00:11:57,341 --> 00:11:58,759
[Trinity] Here's the catch!

240
00:11:59,343 --> 00:12:03,764
The winning group will win one million
in cash!

241
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:05,891
[cheering]

242
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:08,811
And an all-expense paid trip to Europe!

243
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:09,895
[cheering]

244
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,480
[in English] But!

245
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,400
Not only that, not only that.

246
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:20,072
The winners will be invited to perform…

247
00:12:21,031 --> 00:12:26,745
at Mr. Edison Kalaf's 60th birthday bash.

248
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:29,123
[cheering]

249
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:35,171
On his private, members-only island, oh.

250
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:37,214
At Velora Bay!

251
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:38,424
[cheering]

252
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:40,426
- [Trinity] Right?
- [cheering]

253
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:42,136
That's my boss.

254
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:45,097
I mean, he owns this club, so he's rich.

255
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,808
[Trinity, in English]
So, what are you guys waiting for?

256
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:53,772
If you want to join,
this is the last day to register.

257
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:59,361
So, whoever wants to join, go, go, go!

258
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:00,362
[cheering]

259
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:03,157
Let's go, girls! Come on!

260
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,700
[Trinity] Let's party!

261
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:06,202
[cheering]

262
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:09,121
Hey, hey! Come on!

263
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,165
What's attached to them, what is that, eh?

264
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,374
Like it's just fake…

265
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:13,334
[Paldo] I think so too.

266
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:16,170
[upbeat music playing]

267
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:17,338
[chuckles]

268
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:22,051
Why are you looking at me like that, 'Toy?

269
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,014
Do you know how to dance?

270
00:13:27,097 --> 00:13:28,641
Dance? Like this?

271
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,644
Sit down.
We might get accused of something--

272
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:35,064
[Emerson] What, back in…
back in high school, the Tinikling.

273
00:13:35,147 --> 00:13:37,316
The Pandanggo sa Ilaw, the Tinik--

274
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:38,901
No, not in the program.
Not school program.

275
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:40,569
That's all, when I was in school.

276
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,196
Ah, ah-- Atoy, I did ballet.

277
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,281
Ah, in grade three, I did ballet.

278
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:47,159
But I got injured,
so I stopped in grade four. There.

279
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:48,077
Big brother, I do hip-hop.

280
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,537
- Hip-hop?
- [Gavin] Does that work?

281
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,829
- [cool upbeat music playing]
- [clears throat]

282
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:51,747
'Toy.

283
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:54,041
Why, 'Toy? What are you planning?

284
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:56,043
[Trinity, in English]
Come on! Let's party!

285
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:57,878
[audience cheering]

286
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:01,340
[Trinity] Hey, hey! Come on! Come on!

287
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:06,637
Hey, hey! Get up! Come on!

288
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:09,807
Feel beautiful, feel beautiful! Get up!

289
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,392
[music fades]

290
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:13,978
Do your best, huh.

291
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:16,063
[in English] I'm rooting for you, Queen.

292
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:18,440
- Thank you, Queen.
- [drag queen] Good luck.

293
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:20,109
[indistinct chatter]

294
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:22,278
- So? Do you have a dress?
- No!

295
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:24,154
- That won't work, 'Day.
- Lend me a dress.

296
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:26,031
[indistinct chatter]

297
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:27,783
[drag queen] Oh, let's go in.

298
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:31,078
[grunts]

299
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:35,040
We got number seven.

300
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:38,460
So, that means
we still have a few days to prepare.

301
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,170
Huh? What--

302
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:42,006
Ah, ah--

303
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:47,595
Ah, A-- Atoy, you mean we'll…
we'll dress up as drag queens?

304
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:50,389
Yes. That's it, we'll copy them.

305
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,641
We'll perform.

306
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:53,893
But we need to go all out.

307
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:56,437
Really all out so we'll win. That's it.

308
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,397
[Gavin] I think I'll pass.

309
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,481
[sneaky music playing]

310
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:01,317
- What?
- Are you sure about that, Atoy?

311
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,276
Yes!

312
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,861
So, are you game?

313
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:06,906
- [clears throat]
- Keribels or witchikels?

314
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:09,950
What's that? What are you saying?

315
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,535
Keribels, I heard it earlier.

316
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:13,787
"Keribels" means yes. We're game.

317
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:15,664
"Witchikels" means no.

318
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,500
So? Keri? It should be keribels!

319
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:20,711
Uhm, wait--

320
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,172
This seems hard.

321
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:24,840
We're friends, bro, but…

322
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:26,967
It feels…

323
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,344
So? Keribels?

324
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,095
[action music playing]

325
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:32,056
Let's do it, for Ibyang and Janine.

326
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,808
Bro, come on.

327
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:36,060
For the children. Let's do it.

328
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,854
- [Gavin] For the children.
- Come on, come on. For the children.

329
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,649
[others] For the children.

330
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,609
Whoo!

331
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:45,903
Fabulous!

332
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:47,196
Okay. Through the fire!

333
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:50,032
[shouting, cheering]

334
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:53,535
[cheering]

335
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:55,287
Waiter! One more, one more!
Another round! Another round!

336
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:11,553
[pensive music playing]

337
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:19,561
Janine…

338
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,106
Are you okay?

339
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,986
I don't want to be here anymore.
I want to go home.

340
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:33,200
Don't worry.

341
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:36,286
Tatoy will save us.

342
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,788
He's good at finding people and things!

343
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,127
What if he doesn't?

344
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:44,378
What will they do to us?

345
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,171
Will they torture us?

346
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,673
Kill us? Like that?

347
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,134
Don't think about that.

348
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,761
Just say…

349
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:54,805
[somber music playing]

350
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:57,099
Thread through the needle.

351
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:00,185
Pass through, but don't stop.

352
00:17:02,062 --> 00:17:03,605
Tatoy taught me that.

353
00:17:04,898 --> 00:17:08,652
All the… bad thoughts you have,

354
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,654
just let them pass.

355
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:13,949
Like thread through a needle.

356
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,619
[melodramatic music playing]

357
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:20,706
Sorry.

358
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:23,333
It's my fault we got kidnapped.

359
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:26,378
I don't blame you.

360
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:30,382
- [music fades]
- We're allies now, right?

361
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:34,386
[heavy music playing]

362
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:37,598
[in English] Okay. Shoulders, 15.

363
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:40,434
Where is Atoy?

364
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:41,393
[pensive music playing]

365
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,896
Ah, he's out buying fabric.

366
00:17:43,979 --> 00:17:47,691
We need to sew our costumes, eh.

367
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,777
Your biceps. Hmm, are you Popeye?

368
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:50,986
What did you say?

369
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,363
[Cita] You're going to dance at the club?

370
00:17:53,989 --> 00:17:56,450
Eh, this was Atoy's idea.

371
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,912
Hmm, we'll dance and lip-sync like…

372
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:02,790
like drugstore performers.

373
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:05,751
Ah, dra-- drag show performances.

374
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:09,254
In short, we'll glam up
and perform spectacularly.

375
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:10,172
[Emerson] Mmm-hmm.

376
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:11,799
It's not just that.

377
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:14,176
We really need to win.

378
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:17,721
Because that's the easiest way
to get invited to the island

379
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,139
where Janine and Ibyang were taken.

380
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:21,100
[Ame] Ahh.

381
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:24,353
How did you know they were taken there?

382
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:26,730
Yes, Emerson.

383
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,398
- Yes, right?
- [Cita, in English] Thirteen.

384
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:31,193
What if we win and get there?

385
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:34,029
How can we be sure the children
are still there?

386
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:38,242
Of course, we won't go without being sure.

387
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:42,287
Atoy and I already worked out
the info about that place.

388
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:44,123
[men] Cheers! Cheers! Cheers!

389
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,707
[Emerson] Okay. Mm-hmm.

390
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,544
[pleasant music playing]

391
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:49,753
Argh.

392
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,380
- [Paldo] Thank you, Atoy.
- [Atoy] Let's go.

393
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,714
[Nestor] Oh! Thank you, thank you!

394
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:57,970
[muffled chatter]

395
00:18:58,053 --> 00:18:59,555
[Paldo] So, what? More beer.

396
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:00,639
[Uno] All right. You?

397
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:02,474
[muffled chatter]

398
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:08,647
'Son.

399
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,649
[muffled chatter]

400
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:14,903
Attach this to Trinity's collar,
Kalaf's assistant.

401
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,363
Just stick it on.

402
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:18,490
What is this?

403
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:19,908
[muffled chatter]

404
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:22,786
Listening device, a bug.

405
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,872
Stick it anywhere,
as long as it's near the mouth.

406
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:26,999
This is awesome, ah.

407
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:31,128
Like those Double O Seven spy gadgets, ah.

408
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:33,088
[cackles]

409
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,256
There. It's all up to you.

410
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,465
All right. I'll handle it.

411
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:38,177
[muffled chatter]

412
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:40,179
[clears throat]

413
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,396
[drag queen] Huh? A trip?

414
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:50,397
- [Emerson] Hi!
- Europe.

415
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:52,149
Oh, Trinity! Hi!

416
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,026
[in English] Can I take a selfie with you?

417
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:55,819
- Oh, sure! Okay.
- Selfie, yes!

418
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,863
[Emerson laughs] It's a selfie.

419
00:19:58,488 --> 00:20:01,074
- [Emerson, in English] Okay, there you go.
- [Trinity] Okay.

420
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:05,746
- Okay.
- Yep. Another one, another one.

421
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:06,830
Another one! One more, one more.

422
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:07,748
Okay.

423
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:10,334
[action music playing]

424
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:12,294
- There you go, ah!
- Okay. All right!

425
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:13,295
[in English] You don't remember me?

426
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:15,172
You had me make your suit before.

427
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:17,090
[in English] Ah, no. I don't know you.

428
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:18,717
[in English] Ahh! You don't know me?

429
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,801
- I don't know you.
- Ah, you don't know me.

430
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,428
But I know you, you're Trinity!

431
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:22,846
Oh, thank you!

432
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,014
I'm a fan, I'm a fan.

433
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:25,057
Oh, thank you!

434
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,683
Okay, nice. Nice outfit, huh. Okay.

435
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:27,601
Yes. Designer!

436
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:29,478
Wow! I love it!

437
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:31,271
- Okay. Thank you! All right, all right.
- Okay! You take care!

438
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,356
[Emerson] Bye, bye!

439
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,107
[drag queen] Oh, you're so famous.

440
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:35,025
[smirks]

441
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,450
[music fades]

442
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,744
[sneaky music playing]

443
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:51,375
Look at the time.

444
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:53,752
We still haven't picked up
anything important?

445
00:20:53,835 --> 00:20:55,420
We'll be here until morning, eh.

446
00:20:57,923 --> 00:20:59,383
[Trinity on device, in English]
<i>Oh, wait. Excuse me.</i>

447
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,968
<i>I have to take this call.</i>

448
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,640
Hello, Mr. Pullman!

449
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:08,684
He's already there.

450
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,687
He's there,
he's talking to someone on the phone.

451
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:12,771
Yes.

452
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:16,608
[in English] The schedule is confirmed,
and the new fees will be sent by email.

453
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,694
[Trinity on device, in English] <i>Uh-huh.</i>

454
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:21,238
<i>The shipment is by next weekend.</i>

455
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:24,700
<i>On the night of Mr. Kalaf's</i>
<i>birthday celebration.</i>

456
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:25,909
So, you have to come.

457
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:27,536
Yes.

458
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,330
[Trinity on device, in English] <i>The usual,</i>
<i>the shipment will be</i>

459
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:32,040
<i>in transit from Velora Bay.</i>

460
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:35,419
<i>Yes, and the orders will be sorted there…</i>

461
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:38,880
which are women and young children,

462
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:41,466
care of the Black Meridian
and Red Regalia.

463
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:45,804
[Trinity chuckles on device]
<i>Okay, Mr. Pullman.</i> Ciao!

464
00:21:45,887 --> 00:21:48,265
Oh, it seems human trafficking has

465
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:50,434
long been the trade on that island, eh.

466
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:55,939
And, it's like… it's being used
as terrorist training grounds.

467
00:21:56,982 --> 00:21:58,066
[Uno] Exactly.

468
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:00,736
That's why we really need
to expose that place,

469
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:03,196
to stop their illegal business.

470
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:06,575
We really need to get inside that island.

471
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:09,536
Not just for Janine and Ibyang,
but for all the children.

472
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:15,500
But, to get inside and save Ibyang…

473
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:18,003
you need to win
the drag show contest, right?

474
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:22,924
Sis, I don't feel any nerves from you,
you're all straight.

475
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:24,134
How will you do it?

476
00:22:24,217 --> 00:22:28,096
What do you know
about drag show performance?

477
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,347
[Emerson smirks]

478
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:30,932
[sneaky music playing]

479
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:33,351
Miss, I'll handle that.

480
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:34,853
[Karla] Oh.

481
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,064
Wow, give!

482
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:39,566
[henchman] Eat now!

483
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,736
[suspicious music playing]

484
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,655
If I were you, just let us go!

485
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:49,493
If not, our dad will find you
and you'll be in trouble!

486
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:51,244
Stop talking, eat now!

487
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:52,329
[henchman] Hurry up!

488
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:57,876
You're so stubborn, huh!

489
00:22:57,959 --> 00:22:59,252
You think I don't fight back against kids?

490
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:00,962
- What? What?!
- What, huh?! Hmph!

491
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,422
- No, please. No, no.
- [henchman] Huh?

492
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,007
- No-- no, please, no.
- Don't be stubborn, huh.

493
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:05,217
[Ibyang] No, no, please.

494
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,760
- What?!
- You too! You're so stubborn, huh!

495
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:07,928
[Janine] Ibyang!

496
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:09,596
- [henchman] What?
- What's going on?

497
00:23:09,679 --> 00:23:12,015
Boss, she's been like this for a while.
She keeps answering back!

498
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:14,935
You're really bratty even here, huh?

499
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,978
- You need your tongue cut off. [grunts]
- [Janine groans]

500
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:18,313
[Janine] No! [gasps]

501
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:21,024
- We didn't do anything wrong to you!
- [Janine groans]

502
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:24,653
Why do you want to hurt us?!

503
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:25,570
Too bad!

504
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:28,240
Your parents did me wrong!

505
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:29,449
Especially your mother!

506
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:32,661
[sobs] But you're siblings!

507
00:23:33,161 --> 00:23:34,913
I'm your niece!

508
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:37,415
We're family!

509
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:40,710
We should love each other!

510
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:43,964
Why do you want to hurt us?

511
00:23:44,047 --> 00:23:45,966
Family isn't about being related by blood.

512
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:49,094
Your mother infuriates me.

513
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:50,554
Especially when I see you!

514
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:52,222
Especially you!

515
00:23:52,305 --> 00:23:55,225
[tense music playing]

516
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,647
[music fades]

517
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:07,154
[rousing music playing]

518
00:24:13,869 --> 00:24:17,789
[intense music playing]

519
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:23,503
- Hello, ladies!
- [Atoy] Mmm-hmm.

520
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:29,384
[in English] I'm the leader, slash,
choreographer of The Glitter Bombz!

521
00:24:29,467 --> 00:24:31,887
- [Emerson] Oww.
- I'm Antonia.

522
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,138
Oh, we are the…

523
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:33,889
‪UP NEXT

524
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:37,642
- [all] Karayom Kweens!
- [applause]

525
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:41,563
[Chiquita] <i>Amateurs like you</i>
<i>will never take our crown,</i>

526
00:24:41,646 --> 00:24:44,774
and mark that on your ugly foreheads!

527
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:46,151
[exclaims]

528
00:24:46,234 --> 00:24:47,110
[host] Come on!

529
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:49,696
Let's welcome to the stage…

530
00:24:49,779 --> 00:24:53,658
The Karayom Kweens!

531
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:56,912
♪ <i>One cut, and it's done</i> ♪

532
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:58,038
<i>♪ Fix this ♪</i>

533
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,998
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
